<Layout title="About Cyber Reliant"><PageHero eyebrow="ABOUT CYBER RELIANT" title="A different starting point. The file itself." text="Cyber Reliant focuses on protecting sensitive files through a coordinated approach to fragmentation, encryption, distribution and application-level access." number="05"/>
<section class="section container about-statement"><div class="statement-mark" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 180 200"><path d="m15 55 75-40 75 40-75 40zM15 95l75 40 75-40v35l-75 40-75-40z" fill="currentColor"/></svg><span>CYBER RELIANT</span></div><div><span class="eyebrow">THE IDEA AT THE CENTER</span><h2>Infrastructure can change.<br/>The importance of your<br/>information doesn’t.</h2><p class="large-copy">Sensitive data needs protection close to where it lives and how it is used.</p><p>Cyber Reliant’s approach brings the file, its fragments, the cryptographic material and the requesting application into one architectural conversation. The objective is to add a meaningful layer of defense when surrounding systems face compromise.</p><a class="text-link" href="/how-it-works">Understand the approach <Arrow/></a></div></section>
<section class="soft-section"><div class="section container"><span class="eyebrow">PRINCIPLES BEHIND THE APPROACH</span><h2>Designed around what matters.</h2><div class="use-case-grid"><article><span class="card-number">01</span><h3>Start with the data.</h3><p>Consider the sensitive file as a protection boundary, alongside infrastructure and identity controls.</p></article><article><span class="card-number">02</span><h3>Use complementary layers.</h3><p>Bring fragmentation, encryption, distribution, key protection and application controls together.</p></article><article><span class="card-number">03</span><h3>Make room for scrutiny.</h3><p>Evaluate implementation details, operational tradeoffs and evidence for the intended environment.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="section container split-content"><div><span class="eyebrow">THE NEXT CHAPTER</span><h2>Extending the<br/>architecture.</h2></div><div><span class="outline-tag dark-tag">UPCOMING NETWORK VERSION</span><p class="large-copy">An HSM-based key architecture. Multiple logical storage locations. The same focus on sensitive files.</p><p>The planned network version extends the protection approach. Explore the conceptual design, then confirm product availability and deployment details in a technical discussion.</p><a class="text-link" href="/technology#network">Explore what’s next <Arrow/></a></div></section><CTA title="Let’s start a substantive conversation."/></Layout>
